{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1764"},"modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"minimumDominatingSet()","role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (a leaf rule that settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one smaller, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last set found is the answer. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(mean degree d with d² above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the component size in the worst case; the search does not check for task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()"},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"title":"Graph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smaller set is; in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering","title":"Covering","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"title":"Vertex"}}}